committer zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1790621955 +0900

calsync: per-source official sync profiles and delivered_world_all

SyncProfile (frozen) documents the official incremental-sync API each generator source is
modelled on: Calendar events.list(syncToken, 410 GONE), People API connections (7-day sync
tokens, metadata.deleted), Gmail history.list (startHistoryId, 404 after about a week), Tasks
tasks.list(updatedMin, showDeleted), Drive changes.list(pageToken) and Slack
conversations.history(oldest), where a polling client never sees edits or deletions of
messages it already fetched. SyncServer takes a profile; CalendarServer keeps the stage-1
constructor. delivered_world_all runs one server/adapter per source (seed strings include the
source name, calendar keeps its stage-1 seeding) and returns per-source SyncStats; divergence
takes a source. The calendar-only path is byte-identical to before (events, polls, deliveries,
stats and sync params checked on three worlds and three lags).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
